# Migrated from the retired `game-sequence-v1` file of the same name.
# The lines are the authored ones, copied rather than rewritten.

label brom_checks_sword:
    stage sunpetal_crossing
    show brom_copperkeg focused at center
    brom_copperkeg "Hold that training sword level. The edge is harmless, but your grip is trying to wrestle it. A tool works better when you stop asking it to be afraid."
    jump wayfarer_defends_grip

label wayfarer_defends_grip:
    show wayfarer curious at center
    wayfarer "I was trying to look prepared. Is it that obvious this is my first road with monsters on it?"
    jump brom_reframes_monsters

label brom_reframes_monsters:
    brom_copperkeg proud "Story-beasts, not monsters. Most are ordinary neighbors caught in a bad chapter. Drive them off cleanly and leave them a world worth returning to."
    jump wayfarer_notices_charm

label wayfarer_notices_charm:
    wayfarer curious "Is that why you keep a toy windmill beside the forge? It has more careful repairs than some knights have armor."
    jump brom_explains_repairs

label brom_explains_repairs:
    brom_copperkeg worried "A child brought it to me after the first page-storm. Said if the village windmill could forget its turning, hers might teach it again. I could not tell her how frightened that made me."
    jump wayfarer_names_courage

label wayfarer_names_courage:
    wayfarer determined "You repaired it anyway. Perhaps courage is doing careful work while the frightening answer is still unknown."
    jump brom_gives_principle

label brom_gives_principle:
    brom_copperkeg neutral "That is smithing, adventuring, and most decent living. Learn what must be struck, what must be braced, and what only needs time to cool."
    jump wayfarer_accepts_lesson

label wayfarer_accepts_lesson:
    wayfarer delighted "I came for sword advice and received a philosophy. I will try not to swing either one carelessly."
    jump menders_oath_shared

label menders_oath_shared:
    end menders_oath_shared
